slides.content:
`ngModel` lives in `FormsModule`. You must import it in your `AppModule` (or feature module).

```typescript
import { FormsModule } from '@angular/forms';

@NgModule({
  imports: [
    BrowserModule,
    FormsModule  // Add this!
  ],
  ...
})
```
Without it, you’ll get a template parse error.

slides.codeSnippet:
// Textarea
<textarea [(ngModel)]="bio"></textarea>

// Checkbox (boolean)
<input type="checkbox" [(ngModel)]="isSubscribed">

// Select
<select [(ngModel)]="selectedCountry">
  <option value="us">United States</option>
  <option value="uk">United Kingdom</option>
</select>
